## ⚖ Rules Lawyer
Query: "fear_and_dread" rules document for fear save mechanics in Ravenmoor campaign."


The following is the relevant information from the Ravenmoor rulebook regarding Fear and Dread mechanics for fear saves: 

Under 'Fear and Dread', it states: 

'When a character is subjected to a terrifying event, they may suffer from Fear. If a character fails a Will save (DC 15), they suffer from the Frightened condition. This means they must move away from the source of their fear by the shortest route and cannot willingly move towards it.

'Dread' is a more severe form of Fear. When a character suffers from Dread, they take a -4 penalty to all saving throws and are unable to take actions or reactions until they make a successful Will save (DC 20). If the character fails this save, they suffer a permanent decrease in their maximum hit points by 1d3, up to a maximum of their Constitution score. Dread can only be removed by a successful DC 25 Heal check.

